<title>UK: Tibbett in talks to take over Applied.</title>
<headline>Tibbett in talks to take over Applied.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British transport and distribution firm Tibbett &amp; Britten Group Plc said on Friday that it was in talks that could lead to an all-share offer for Applied Distribution Group Plc.</p>
<p>Tibbett said the offer, if it materialised, would value each Applied Disribution share at about 48 pence each.  </p>
<p>At 48p a share, a bid would be worth around 17 million stg.</p>
<p>Close Brothers Corporate Finance Ltd is advising Tibbett &amp; Britten, the company said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
